The ML evaluation/status vertical slice is complete and fully validated. Final report:

## What was already working

The repository already had the complete stack: ESP32 firmware → ADS1115/DS18B20 → MQTT → FastAPI ingestion (retry de-dup, validation) → PostgreSQL → live ML inference (Isolation Forest + Random Forest at ingest) → authority dashboard AI panels. That was validated in earlier sessions: 116 backend tests, 41 frontend tests, live broker round-trip, commit `ee81d35`.

## What was implemented this session

The missing pieces were **machine-readable evaluation artifacts, a model-status API, and dashboard visibility of real metrics**:

**1. Evaluation report generator** — [build_evaluation_report.py](ml/scripts/build_evaluation_report.py) loads the saved artifacts, scores the held-out test splits, and writes [evaluation_report.json](ml/reports/evaluation_report.json) + [evaluation_report.md](ml/reports/evaluation_report.md). Every metric is computed at generation time; nothing is hardcoded.

**2. Backend API** — [ml_status_service.py](backend/app/services/ml_status_service.py), [ml_status.py](backend/app/schemas/ml_status.py) schemas, and `GET /api/authority/ml/status` in [authority.py:29](backend/app/api/v1/authority.py#L29) (authority-only). Missing/corrupt reports return `evaluation_available: false` with `evaluation: null` — never placeholder numbers. Only public metadata is exposed (file names, never absolute paths).

**3. Dashboard card** — [ModelHealthCard.tsx](frontend/src/components/authority/ModelHealthCard.tsx) on the Analytics page with per-model load badges (Loaded / Not loaded / Missing artifact), real RF + IF metrics, the limitations list, and explicit loading / error / unauthorized / "report not generated" states (the last names the regeneration command). Types + `authorityApi.getMlStatus` added to [api.ts](frontend/src/lib/api.ts).

**4. Docs** — README gained the report command, endpoint row, and a "Model health & evaluation transparency" section; [ml/README.md](ml/README.md) gained pipeline step 8.

**5. Bug fix** — [run_server.py](backend/run_server.py) exited with code 3 under the installed uvicorn (`reload=True` requires an import string); it now starts the server as the README documents.

## Actual metrics (from the executed report)

| Model | Metric | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Random Forest | Accuracy / F1-macro / ROC-AUC on 15,120 held-out benchmark samples | 99.99% / 99.98% / ~100% |
| Isolation Forest | Readings scored / flagged / rate | 9 / 4 / 44.4% (no ground-truth labels — accuracy intentionally not reported) |
| XGBoost | Accuracy vs balanced accuracy (1,139 USGS test samples) | 94.4% vs **53.8%** — honest, class-skewed; offline-only |

