## 8. ESP32 → MQTT → backend → frontend data flow

```text
ADS1115(I²C 21/22) A0 pH, A1 TDS, A2 turbidity(divider)   DS18B20(GPIO 4)
        │ 7/7/10-sample averages, ±4.096 V gain
        ▼
readPh() / readTds() / readTurbidity() / readTemperature()   [hydrasense_esp32.ino]
        │ invalid → JSON null + diagnostics.*.error  (never fabricated)
        ▼
publishTelemetry() ── topic: hydrasense/stations/<STATION_CODE>/telemetry
        │ payload: {station_code, device_id, timestamp(ISO-8601 UTC, NTP-gated),
        │           pH, pH_status, turbidity, turbidity_status, turbidity_unit,
        │           tds, temperature, source:"esp32",
        │           diagnostics:{ph,turbidity,tds,temperature,device{uptime_ms,wifi_rssi_dbm,seq,errors}}}
        ▼  QoS 1, 3 s cadence (PUBLISH_INTERVAL_MS)
Mosquitto :1883 (anonymous, LAN)  ◄── simulator publishes the same topic with source:"simulator",
        ▼                             turbidity_unit:"ntu"
MQTTSubscriberService  topic filter "hydrasense/stations/+/telemetry"   [mqtt_service.py]
        on_message → process_telemetry_payload()
          1. json.loads → 2. validate_telemetry_payload() (required fields, ISO timestamp with time
             component, physical ranges, bool rejection, turbidity unit/status grammar, source pattern,
             diagnostics ≤8 KiB)  → 3. station_code lookup (unknown → reject)
          4. duplicate guard on (station_id, device_id, timestamp) → skip
          5. INSERT sensor_readings (NULLs preserved, turbidity_unit/status/index, source, diagnostics)
          6. assess_reading() → persist_assessments()  → water_suitability_assessments
          7. if unit==relative_index OR any of the 4 values NULL → skip ML (logged reason)
             else attach_ml_results() → anomaly_*/water_quality_* columns on the same row
        ▼
REST  /api/public/...        (anonymous: station, latest, history, suitability)
      /api/authority/...     (JWT + AUTHORITY: readings, live-assessment, forecast, ML analysis, alerts)
      /api/product/...       (JWT + PRODUCT_USER: overview, tests, alerts, activate)
      /api/simulation/...    (lease-guarded start/pause/generate)
        ▼
React  lib/api.ts (VITE_API_BASE_URL → http://127.0.0.1:8000/api)
      TelemetryStatusCard / LiveMonitoring / TestResult / PublicSource …
```

**Missing/stale/disconnected handling, end to end:** firmware defers publishing until NTP syncs (no 1970 timestamps) and reports device errors after a successful uplink; backend stores NULL and never coerces it; freshness is computed server-side (`fresh` / `delayed` / `stale`, [water_suitability.py](backend/app/services/water_suitability.py)); the UI shows *Uncalibrated*/*Sensor failed* tiles, an Online/Stale/Offline link badge, provenance badges, and collapses assessments to `insufficient_data` for missing/stale/unstable values. **Implemented**.

