## 10. Dashboard and water-quality assessment logic

**Where assessments come from:** one central engine — [suitability_engine.py](backend/app/services/suitability_engine.py) (facade, rejects any input key outside `ph/tds/temperature/turbidity` with `ValueError`) → [water_screening.py](backend/app/services/water_screening.py) per-purpose profiles (`CRITERIA_VERSION`, drinking/domestic/irrigation/swimming/aquaculture/general), plus the standards-based [water_suitability.py](backend/app/services/water_suitability.py) used at ingestion and on public/authority endpoints. Canonical states: `within_configured_ranges` / `caution` / `outside_configured_ranges` / `insufficient_data` ([screening_states.py](backend/app/services/screening_states.py)).

**Frontend rendering:** `TestResult.tsx`, `LiveMonitoring.tsx` and `UserDashboard.tsx` render the **backend's** result — `overall.status`, `overall.label/summary`, `reason_details`, `reasons`, `attention[]`, `limitations[]`, `next_steps[]`, `data_quality.{calibration_status, freshness, stability, demo_mode, errors, warnings}` — plus an explicit "*Preliminary screening only … not a laboratory safety certification*" banner and the turbidity `not_comparable` note. Stability comes from the backend (`sensor_stability.py`, 10 valid samples over 20 s, per-parameter tolerances). Missing values render as `—`/`Uncalibrated`, never as numbers. **Implemented**, and consistent between API and UI (frontend tests assert label agreement).

**Drinking-water wording:** the backend never certifies safety — results carry BIS-referenced *screening* language plus missing-parameter lists (microbiology/chemicals), and pH+TDS passing with an uncalibrated turbidity index is capped at `caution` with an "NTU calibration required" reason. **Implemented**.

