## 4. Sensor and ADC pin mapping

From [hydrasense_esp32.ino:41–54](firmware/hydrasense_esp32/hydrasense_esp32.ino#L41) and the wiring table in [firmware/README.md](firmware/README.md):

| Sensor | Interface | Channel / pin | Conversion path | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Analog pH module | ADS1115 single-ended | **A0** (`CH_PH 0`) | 7-sample average @8 ms → counts×LSB (±4.096 V) → one-point pH formula | **Implemented** (calibration wrong — §5) |
| Analog TDS module | ADS1115 single-ended | **A1** (`CH_TDS 1`), **no divider** (direct `"A"` output) | 7-sample average → volts → `tdsConvert()` linear ppm | **Partially implemented** (provisional, uncompensated — §6) |
| DS18B20 temperature | OneWire | **GPIO 4** + 4.7 kΩ pull-up | `getTempCByIndex(0)`; rejects −127 °C (disconnect) and 85 °C (power-up default) | **Implemented** |
| Analog turbidity module | ADS1115 single-ended | **A2** (`CH_TURBIDITY 2`) through the **existing 10 kΩ/20 kΩ divider** | 10-sample average @2 ms → ×(R1+R2)/R2 = ×1.5 back to sensor-OUT volts → 0.400 V "clear" … 0.100 V "cloudy" mapped to index 0–100 | **Implemented** (relative index only, never NTU) |
| ADS1115 | I²C | **SDA GPIO 21, SCL GPIO 22**, addr 0x48, `GAIN_ONE` (±4.096 V) | `ads.begin()` failure → all analog values publish `null` + a `device.errors` entry | **Implemented** |
| ESP32's own ADC | — | **unused** (GPIO 32/34/35 free) | — | **Implemented** |

**Filtering/averaging:** pH and TDS average 7 samples 8 ms apart; turbidity averages 10 samples 20 ms apart. No median or low-pass beyond that. **Implemented**.

**Disconnect / invalid handling (firmware):** ADS missing → `hasValue=false` + error string; pH voltage outside 0.01–3.25 V or estimated pH outside 0–14 → JSON `null` + error (never clamped); turbidity sensor-OUT < 0.02 V → `null` (never index 100); DS18B20 −127/≥85 → `null` + `"valid":false`. **Implemented**.

**Backend handling:** `validate_telemetry_payload()` accepts JSON `null` for any sensor, rejects non-numeric/out-of-range values, malformed timestamps, malformed turbidity units/status and bad source tags ([mqtt_service.py:109–175](backend/app/services/mqtt_service.py#L109)). NULLs are stored as NULL, never defaulted to 0. **Implemented**.

**Frontend handling:** `TelemetryStatusCard` renders NULL as `"Uncalibrated"` / `"Sensor failed"`, shows raw ADC, voltage, calibration badge, RSSI, uptime, sequence and device errors ([TelemetryStatusCard.tsx:152–153](frontend/src/components/authority/TelemetryStatusCard.tsx#L152)); link badge Online <15 s / Stale <5 min / Offline. **Implemented**.

