Lab notification now actually sends the report to the lab by email, and there's finally a way to trigger it from the app.

**What the backend already did, and what I fixed in it** — `POST /api/authority/incidents/{id}/notify-lab` already composed the incident PDF and SMTP-mailed it to the chosen lab contact. Two real defects blocked it:

- **The operator's note never reached the lab.** It was only stored in the internal audit trail. It's now appended to the email body under "Message from the reporting authority", so the lab sees why the sample was sent.
- **A failed delivery could never be retried.** `notify_lab` recorded `lab_notified` and then tried the same transition again, so every retry returned `409 invalid_transition` — meaning a transient SMTP outage left the incident permanently un-notifiable. A re-send on an already-notified incident now records an audit event (`Re-notification: … Report delivery: sent|failed`) without a duplicate status change.

**Frontend** — the Incidents page was mock data only, so the email flow had no trigger. It now runs on the real API: incident queue with delivery badges, a detail pane with the workflow timeline, a lab-contact picker plus optional note, and an "Email report to lab" button. Delivery states are shown exactly as the API reports them — **sent** (green, with recipient and time), **smtp_unconfigured** (amber, "NO email was sent…" plus a Download PDF button for manual delivery), **failed** (red, retry stays enabled). No "sent" is ever shown for a message that didn't leave the server.

